---
import PluginLayout from '../../layouts/PluginLayout.astro';
import pluginsData from '../../data/plugins.json';
// Colors from logo: gold #f0aa22 (gear/coins), deep amber #c47c0a (frame)
const p = pluginsData.find(x => x.name === 'GearFlow')!;
---
<PluginLayout
  title="GearFlow — Modular Inventory, Equipment & Crafting Plugin for UE5"
  description="A fully modular inventory, equipment, and crafting system for Unreal Engine 5. Data-driven items with opt-in fragments, flat recipe data assets, and tag-driven gear slots — multiplayer-ready and extensible per project."
  pluginName="GearFlow"
  version={p.version}
  coverImage={p.cover}
  logoImage={p.logo}
  fabUrl={p.fabUrl ?? '#'}
  accent={p.accent}
  accentLight={p.accentLight}
  bg="#0a0802"
  surface="#130e04"
  surface2="#1c1508"
  codeBg="#080601"
>

  <!-- ── Sidebar nav ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <nav slot="sidebar-nav">
    <div class="nav-group">
      <span class="nav-group-label">Introduction</span>
      <a href="#overview">Overview</a>
      <a href="#getting-started">Getting Started</a>
    </div>
    <div class="nav-group">
      <span class="nav-group-label">Items</span>
      <a href="#item-definition">Item Definition</a>
      <a href="#item-instance">Item Instance</a>
    </div>
    <div class="nav-group">
      <span class="nav-group-label">Storage</span>
      <a href="#storage-component">Storage Component</a>
      <a href="#inventory-component">Inventory</a>
      <a href="#equipment-component">Equipment</a>
      <a href="#wallet-component">Wallet</a>
    </div>
    <div class="nav-group">
      <span class="nav-group-label">Crafting</span>
      <a href="#crafting-component">Crafting Component</a>
      <a href="#recipes">Recipes</a>
    </div>
    <div class="nav-group">
      <span class="nav-group-label">World</span>
      <a href="#loot-tables">Loot Tables</a>
      <a href="#pickup-actor">Pickup Actor</a>
      <a href="#transfer-system">Transfer System</a>
    </div>
    <div class="nav-group">
      <span class="nav-group-label">Multiplayer</span>
      <a href="#multiplayer">Replication</a>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <!-- ── Overview ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="doc-section" id="overview" data-section="overview">
    <h2 class="doc-section-title">
      <span class="section-icon">
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"/><line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"/></svg>
      </span>
      Overview
    </h2>
    <div class="section-divider"></div>
    <p class="doc-p">
      <strong>GearFlow</strong> is a modular inventory, equipment, and crafting framework for Unreal Engine 5. Items are <strong>UGearItemDefinition</strong> data assets — a small core of flat fields (name, description, icon) plus an opt-in <strong>Fragments</strong> array. Each fragment owns one concern: stacking rules live on <code>UGearStackFragment</code>, equipment slot data on <code>UGearEquipmentFragment</code>, purchase cost on <code>UGearCostFragment</code>, and world pickup visuals on <code>UGearPickupFragment</code>. A simple sword asset carries only the fragments it actually needs — nothing more is allocated.
    </p>
    <p class="doc-p">
      Three storage components — <strong>Inventory</strong>, <strong>Equipment</strong>, and <strong>Wallet</strong> — extend a shared <strong>UGearStorageComponent</strong> base that owns the replicated slot array and the full Add/Remove/Query API. A world-facing layer of pickup actors, loot tables, and a unified <strong>TransferItem</strong> model covers every item-movement pattern without custom code. GAS is optional.
    </p>

    <div class="feature-grid">
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/></svg>
        </div>
        <p class="feature-title">Fragment System</p>
        <p class="feature-desc">Item behaviour is composed via opt-in fragments — stacking, equipment slots, cost, and world pickups each live on their own fragment class. Add only what each item needs; nothing extra is allocated.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="2" y="7" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/><path d="M16 7V5a2 2 0 0 0-2-2h-4a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v2"/></svg>
        </div>
        <p class="feature-title">Modular Components</p>
        <p class="feature-desc">Add only what each actor needs. A chest uses Inventory. A player adds Equipment. A shop NPC adds Wallet. Each component is self-contained.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M17 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H5a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/><path d="M23 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"/><path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"/></svg>
        </div>
        <p class="feature-title">Multiplayer Ready</p>
        <p class="feature-desc">FastArray replication with delta compression on all storage components. Server-authoritative. Works with Listen and Dedicated servers out of the box.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="16 18 22 12 16 6"/><polyline points="8 6 2 12 8 18"/></svg>
        </div>
        <p class="feature-title">Designer Friendly</p>
        <p class="feature-desc">All items, recipes, and loot tables are data assets. Designers create and iterate entirely in the Content Browser, no C++ required.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M8 3H5a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v3m18 0V5a2 2 0 0 0-2-2h-3M3 16v3a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h3m8 0h3a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-3"/></svg>
        </div>
        <p class="feature-title">Transfer Model</p>
        <p class="feature-desc">All item movement — looting, buying, dropping — runs through UGearFunctionLibrary. One unified path, one set of delegates, no custom movement code.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14.7 6.3a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.4l1.6 1.6a1 1 0 0 0 1.4 0l3.77-3.77a6 6 0 0 1-7.94 7.94l-6.91 6.91a2.12 2.12 0 0 1-3-3l6.91-6.91a6 6 0 0 1 7.94-7.94l-3.76 3.76z"/></svg>
        </div>
        <p class="feature-title">Crafting System</p>
        <p class="feature-desc">Data-driven recipes with multi-output support. A CraftingRule object handles custom validation — positional grids, skill gates, or anything else.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>
        </div>
        <p class="feature-title">Equipment Slots</p>
        <p class="feature-desc">Tag-driven named gear slots. Items carry a <code>UGearEquipmentFragment</code> that declares accepted slot types and an optional visual actor class; the Equipment Component matches and spawns it on equip.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/><path d="M19.07 4.93a10 10 0 0 1 0 14.14"/><path d="M4.93 4.93a10 10 0 0 0 0 14.14"/></svg>
        </div>
        <p class="feature-title">World Pickup Actors</p>
        <p class="feature-desc">Items with a <code>UGearPickupFragment</code> can be dropped into the world. <code>UGearFunctionLibrary::DropItem</code> spawns the configured pickup actor class, auto-picks up on overlap, and supports Timed or Persistent lifetimes.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="callout callout-info">
      <span class="callout-icon">
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"/><line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"/></svg>
      </span>
      <span>GearFlow does not require the Gameplay Ability System. It integrates well with GAS — the optional <strong>EquipmentRule</strong> object and custom fragment subclasses are natural GAS extension points — but GAS is entirely optional.</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Getting Started ────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="doc-section" id="getting-started" data-section="getting-started">
    <h2 class="doc-section-title">
      <span class="section-icon">
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polygon points="5 3 19 12 5 21 5 3"/></svg>
      </span>
      Getting Started
    </h2>
    <div class="section-divider"></div>
    <p class="doc-p">A working inventory is up and running in five steps. The fastest path requires no C++ beyond adding the module dependency.</p>

    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step">
        <span class="step-num">1</span>
        <div class="step-body">
          <p class="step-title">Enable the plugin</p>
          <p class="step-desc">In the Unreal Editor, open <strong>Edit → Plugins</strong>, search for <em>GearFlow</em>, and enable it. Restart the editor when prompted.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <span class="step-num">2</span>
        <div class="step-body">
          <p class="step-title">Add the module dependency</p>
          <p class="step-desc">Open your project's <strong>Build.cs</strong> and add <code>"GearFlow"</code> to <code>PublicDependencyModuleNames</code>. This gives access to all GearFlow C++ headers in your module.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <span class="step-num">3</span>
        <div class="step-body">
          <p class="step-title">Create an Item Definition</p>
          <p class="step-desc">Right-click in the Content Browser and select <strong>GearFlow → Item Definition</strong>. Open the asset and set <strong>DisplayName</strong> and <strong>Icon</strong>. Add fragments to the <strong>Fragments</strong> array as needed — for example, a <code>UGearEquipmentFragment</code> to make the item equippable, or a <code>UGearStackFragment</code> to allow stacking.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <span class="step-num">4</span>
        <div class="step-body">
          <p class="step-title">Add UGearInventoryComponent to your character</p>
          <p class="step-desc">In your character Blueprint or C++, add a <strong>UGearInventoryComponent</strong> and set <code>SlotCount</code> to the number of inventory slots you want. No further setup is required — the component replicates automatically.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <span class="step-num">5</span>
        <div class="step-body">
          <p class="step-title">Add an item</p>
          <p class="step-desc">Call <code>AddItem(ItemDefinition, Count)</code> on the component from the server. The item fills existing stacks first (for stackable items), then creates new slots. Replication to clients is automatic — no extra RPC code needed.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Item Definition ────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="doc-section" id="item-definition" data-section="item-definition">
    <h2 class="doc-section-title">
      <span class="section-icon">
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/></svg>
      </span>
      Item Definition
    </h2>
    <div class="section-divider"></div>
    <p class="doc-p">
      <strong>UGearItemDefinition</strong> extends <code>UPrimaryDataAsset</code> and is the immutable definition for an item type. It is never modified at runtime — it is the template from which instances are created. A small set of flat fields is present on every item; all optional behaviour is added via the <strong>Fragments</strong> array.
    </p>

    <table class="prop-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Property</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td class="prop-name">DisplayName</td>
          <td class="prop-type">FText</td>
          <td class="prop-desc">Shown in inventory UI.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="prop-name">Description</td>
          <td class="prop-type">FText</td>
          <td class="prop-desc">Tooltip or detail panel text.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="prop-name">Icon</td>
          <td class="prop-type">TSoftObjectPtr&lt;UTexture2D&gt;</td>
          <td class="prop-desc">Inventory slot icon. Soft reference — loaded on demand, not held in memory when the item is not displayed.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="prop-name">Fragments</td>
          <td class="prop-type">TArray&lt;UGearItemFragment*&gt;</td>
          <td class="prop-desc">Instanced fragment objects that attach optional behaviour to this item — stacking, equipment slots, cost, pickup visuals, or any custom fragment defined in your project.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <div class="doc-subsection">
      <h3 class="doc-subsection-title">Fragment Types</h3>
      <p class="doc-p" style="margin-bottom:12px">Each fragment is an instanced <code>UGearItemFragment</code> subclass added to the <strong>Fragments</strong> array in the editor. The absence of a fragment means the item simply does not have that capability — no stub code, no null-checks on unused properties.</p>

      <table class="prop-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Fragment Class</th><th>Property</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name" rowspan="1">UGearStackFragment</td>
            <td class="prop-name">MaxStackSize</td>
            <td class="prop-type">int32</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">Maximum units allowed per inventory slot. Minimum 2. Absence of this fragment means the item is non-stackable — each unit gets its own instance.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name" rowspan="2">UGearEquipmentFragment</td>
            <td class="prop-name">AcceptedSlotTypes</td>
            <td class="prop-type">FGameplayTagContainer</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">Tags matched against a slot's <code>SlotFilter</code>. An item fits a slot when at least one tag matches. Absence of this fragment means the item cannot be equipped.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name">EquippedVisualClass</td>
            <td class="prop-type">TSoftClassPtr&lt;AActor&gt;</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">Actor class spawned and attached to the character when this item is equipped. Null means no visual is spawned. Replicated to all clients.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name" rowspan="1">UGearCostFragment</td>
            <td class="prop-name">Cost</td>
            <td class="prop-type">TMap&lt;FGameplayTag, int32&gt;</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">Currency tag → amount pairs. Used by <code>TransferItem</code> when a wallet is provided — the transfer fails atomically if the wallet cannot cover all entries. Absence means the item transfers freely.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name" rowspan="2">UGearPickupFragment</td>
            <td class="prop-name">PickupActorClass</td>
            <td class="prop-type">TSoftClassPtr&lt;AGearPickupActor&gt;</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">Actor class spawned when this item is dropped. Null uses the built-in <code>AGearStaticMeshPickupActor</code>. Override with a project subclass for custom visuals or behaviour. Absence of this fragment means the item cannot be dropped.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name">WorldMesh</td>
            <td class="prop-type">TSoftObjectPtr&lt;UStaticMesh&gt;</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">Mesh applied to <code>AGearStaticMeshPickupActor</code> when dropped. Ignored if <code>PickupActorClass</code> is set to a custom actor.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Item Instance ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="doc-section" id="item-instance" data-section="item-instance">
    <h2 class="doc-section-title">
      <span class="section-icon">
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2"/><path d="M9 9h6M9 12h6M9 15h4"/></svg>
      </span>
      Item Instance
    </h2>
    <div class="section-divider"></div>
    <p class="doc-p">
      <strong>UGearItemInstance</strong> is the runtime handle for an item occupying a slot. It holds a pointer to the immutable definition. Stackable items share one instance per slot with the count tracked separately in the slot struct; non-stackable items have one instance per unit so each can carry individual state. Instances are owned and replicated by the storage component — never construct one manually, always interact through the component API. The class is Blueprint-subclassable for per-item state such as durability or enchantments.
    </p>

    <table class="prop-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Property</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td class="prop-name">Definition</td>
          <td class="prop-type">UGearItemDefinition*</td>
          <td class="prop-desc">The definition this instance was created from. Replicated.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <table class="prop-table" style="margin-top:16px">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Function</th><th>Returns</th><th>Description</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td class="prop-name">GetDefinition()</td>
          <td class="prop-type">UGearItemDefinition*</td>
          <td class="prop-desc">Inline getter for the definition.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="prop-name">IsStackable()</td>
          <td class="prop-type">bool</td>
          <td class="prop-desc">Whether this item can stack — true when the definition carries a <code>UGearStackFragment</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="prop-name">FindFragmentByClass(FragmentClass)</td>
          <td class="prop-type">UGearItemFragment*</td>
          <td class="prop-desc">Convenience passthrough to <code>Definition->FindFragmentByClass</code>. Use in Blueprint graphs to access fragment data from an instance.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="prop-name">OnInstanceCreated()</td>
          <td class="prop-type">Blueprint event</td>
          <td class="prop-desc">Called once after <code>Definition</code> is assigned. Override to initialize per-instance state such as randomized durability on first creation.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="prop-name">GetInstanceSaveData(out TMap&lt;FString,FString&gt;)</td>
          <td class="prop-type">Blueprint event</td>
          <td class="prop-desc">Return custom key/value pairs representing this instance's state for save serialization.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="prop-name">SetInstanceSaveData(TMap&lt;FString,FString&gt;)</td>
          <td class="prop-type">Blueprint event</td>
          <td class="prop-desc">Restore custom save data on load. Called before <code>OnInstanceCreated</code> when loading from save.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Storage Component ──────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="doc-section" id="storage-component" data-section="storage-component">
    <h2 class="doc-section-title">
      <span class="section-icon">
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="2" y="7" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/><path d="M16 7V5a2 2 0 0 0-2-2h-4a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v2"/></svg>
      </span>
      Storage Component
    </h2>
    <div class="section-divider"></div>
    <p class="doc-p">
      <strong>UGearStorageComponent</strong> is the abstract base shared by Inventory and Equipment. It owns the replicated slot array (<code>FGearContainerSlotArray</code> via FastArray) and exposes the full Add/Remove/Query API. All mutating functions are server-authoritative — calling them on a client has no effect.
    </p>

    <div class="doc-subsection">
      <h3 class="doc-subsection-title">FGearContainerSlot</h3>
      <table class="prop-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name">SlotFilter</td>
            <td class="prop-type">FGameplayTag</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">Matched against the item's <code>UGearEquipmentFragment.AcceptedSlotTypes</code>. An empty tag accepts any item.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name">Instance</td>
            <td class="prop-type">UGearItemInstance*</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">The item instance occupying this slot. <code>nullptr</code> if empty.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name">Count</td>
            <td class="prop-type">int32</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">Stack count for stackable items. Always 1 for non-stackable items.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name">bStackable</td>
            <td class="prop-type">bool</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">Whether this slot allows stacking. Set during component initialization.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name">MaxStackSize</td>
            <td class="prop-type">int32</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">Maximum stack count for this slot.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-subsection">
      <h3 class="doc-subsection-title">Functions</h3>
      <table class="prop-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Function</th><th>Description</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">AddItem(Definition, Count)</td><td class="prop-desc">Adds Count units; fills existing stacks first, then new slots. Returns the amount actually added. Server only.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">AddItemInstance(Instance)</td><td class="prop-desc">Places a pre-created instance into the first available matching slot. Server only.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">RemoveItem(Definition, Count)</td><td class="prop-desc">Removes Count units by item type. Returns false if insufficient. Server only.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">RemoveItemInstance(Instance)</td><td class="prop-desc">Removes a specific instance. Server only.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">ClearAllItems()</td><td class="prop-desc">Removes all items from all slots. Server only.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">RestoreSlotState(SlotIndex, Definition, Count)</td><td class="prop-desc">Reconstructs a slot from save data without going through the normal add path.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">SwapSlots(IndexA, IndexB)</td><td class="prop-desc">Swaps two slots within this component.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">SwapSlotsBetween(IndexA, OtherComponent, IndexB)</td><td class="prop-desc">Swaps a slot in this component with a slot in another component.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">ConsolidateStacks()</td><td class="prop-desc">Merges split stacks of the same item where possible, freeing slots.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">GetItemCount(Definition)</td><td class="prop-desc">Returns total units of an item across all slots.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">HasItem(Definition, Count)</td><td class="prop-desc">Returns true if at least Count units of the item are present.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">CanAddItem(Definition, Count)</td><td class="prop-desc">Returns true if there is room to add Count units without losing any.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">GetItemInstance(Definition)</td><td class="prop-desc">Returns the first instance of the given item type, or nullptr.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">GetSlots()</td><td class="prop-desc">Returns all slots as an array snapshot. Safe to call on client.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">FindAvailableSlotIndex(Definition)</td><td class="prop-desc">Returns the index of the first available slot for the item, or -1 if none.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-subsection">
      <h3 class="doc-subsection-title">Delegates</h3>
      <table class="prop-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Delegate</th><th>Parameters</th><th>Description</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name">OnSlotChanged</td>
            <td class="prop-type">SlotIndex, FGearContainerSlot</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">Fires on any slot mutation — add, remove, or stack count change. Broadcasts on both server and client after replication. Bind here to keep UI in sync.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name">OnStorageFull</td>
            <td class="prop-type">Item, AmountNotAdded</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">Fires when <code>AddItem</code> cannot place all units due to capacity. Use to show a "Inventory Full" notification.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Inventory Component ────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="doc-section" id="inventory-component" data-section="inventory-component">
    <h2 class="doc-section-title">
      <span class="section-icon">
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="2" y="7" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/><path d="M16 7V5a2 2 0 0 0-2-2h-4a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v2"/><line x1="12" y1="12" x2="12" y2="16"/><line x1="10" y1="14" x2="14" y2="14"/></svg>
      </span>
      Inventory Component
    </h2>
    <div class="section-divider"></div>
    <p class="doc-p">
      <strong>UGearInventoryComponent</strong> extends <code>UGearStorageComponent</code> and acts as the player bag, chest, or loot container. It configures the slot array at initialization time using the properties below — all slot stacking rules are established once and do not change at runtime.
    </p>

    <table class="prop-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Property</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td class="prop-name">SlotCount</td>
          <td class="prop-type">int32</td>
          <td class="prop-desc">Total number of inventory slots created on initialization.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="prop-name">bDefaultStackable</td>
          <td class="prop-type">bool</td>
          <td class="prop-desc">Applied to all slots on init unless overridden per-slot via <code>SlotFilters</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="prop-name">DefaultMaxStackSize</td>
          <td class="prop-type">int32</td>
          <td class="prop-desc">Default max stack count when <code>bDefaultStackable</code> is true.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="prop-name">SlotFilters</td>
          <td class="prop-type">TArray&lt;FGameplayTag&gt;</td>
          <td class="prop-desc">Per-slot tag filters at init, index-matched to the slot array. Slots without an entry in this array use an empty filter (accepts anything).</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <div class="callout callout-info">
      <span class="callout-icon">
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"/><line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"/></svg>
      </span>
      <span>All mutating functions from <code>UGearStorageComponent</code> — <code>AddItem</code>, <code>RemoveItem</code>, <code>SwapSlots</code> — are available on this component. Calling them from a non-authority client has no effect; always call from the server or use the provided Server RPCs (<code>Server_AddItem</code>, <code>Server_RemoveItem</code>).</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Equipment Component ───────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="doc-section" id="equipment-component" data-section="equipment-component">
    <h2 class="doc-section-title">
      <span class="section-icon">
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>
      </span>
      Equipment Component
    </h2>
    <div class="section-divider"></div>
    <p class="doc-p">
      <strong>UGearEquipmentComponent</strong> extends <code>UGearStorageComponent</code> and manages named gear slots — one item per slot. Only items that carry a <code>UGearEquipmentFragment</code> can be equipped; the fragment's <code>AcceptedSlotTypes</code> is matched against the slot tag. When an item is equipped, the component spawns the fragment's <code>EquippedVisualClass</code> actor server-side, attaches it to the specified socket on <code>VisualAttachTarget</code>, and replicates the visual actor to all clients. Unequipping destroys the visual actor.
    </p>

    <div class="doc-subsection">
      <h3 class="doc-subsection-title">Properties</h3>
      <table class="prop-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Property</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name">EquipmentSlotDefinitions</td>
            <td class="prop-type">TArray&lt;FGameplayTag&gt;</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">The set of valid slot tags (e.g. <code>Equipment.Weapon.MainHand</code>). Only tags listed here are recognized as equipment slots.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name">VisualAttachTarget</td>
            <td class="prop-type">USceneComponent*</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">Component to attach visual actors to — typically the character's skeletal mesh.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name">SlotAttachSockets</td>
            <td class="prop-type">TMap&lt;FGameplayTag, FName&gt;</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">Maps slot tag to socket name on <code>VisualAttachTarget</code>. If a slot has no entry, the visual attaches at the component root.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name">EquipmentRule</td>
            <td class="prop-type">UGearEquipmentRule*</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">Optional custom validation object. Default validation is tag matching only. Subclass <code>UGearEquipmentRule</code> to add level requirements, class restrictions, or other conditions.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-subsection">
      <h3 class="doc-subsection-title">Functions</h3>
      <table class="prop-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Function</th><th>Description</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">EquipItem(Definition, SlotTag)</td><td class="prop-desc">Equips by item definition; creates a new instance. Requires a <code>UGearEquipmentFragment</code> with a matching slot tag. Unequips the current occupant if needed. Server only.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">EquipItemInstance(Instance, SlotTag)</td><td class="prop-desc">Equips a pre-existing instance into the specified slot. Server only.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">UnequipSlot(SlotTag)</td><td class="prop-desc">Removes the item from the slot; does not destroy the instance. Server only.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">UnequipItem(Definition)</td><td class="prop-desc">Finds and unequips the first slot holding this item type. Server only.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">UnequipItemInstance(Instance)</td><td class="prop-desc">Unequips a specific instance. Server only.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">GetItemInSlot(SlotTag)</td><td class="prop-desc">Returns the <code>UGearItemDefinition*</code> in that slot, or nullptr if empty.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">GetItemInstanceInSlot(SlotTag)</td><td class="prop-desc">Returns the <code>UGearItemInstance*</code> in that slot, or nullptr.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">IsSlotOccupied(SlotTag)</td><td class="prop-desc">Returns true if the slot has an item.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">GetEquippedItems()</td><td class="prop-desc">Returns a <code>TMap&lt;FGameplayTag, UGearItemDefinition*&gt;</code> of all occupied slots.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">GetSlotVisual(SlotTag)</td><td class="prop-desc">Returns the live spawned visual actor for that slot, or nullptr if the slot is empty or the item's <code>UGearEquipmentFragment</code> has no <code>EquippedVisualClass</code>.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-subsection">
      <h3 class="doc-subsection-title">Delegates</h3>
      <table class="prop-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Delegate</th><th>Parameters</th><th>Description</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name">OnItemEquipped</td>
            <td class="prop-type">SlotTag, Instance</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">Fires after equip replication reaches clients. Safe to use for UI and VFX responses.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name">OnItemUnequipped</td>
            <td class="prop-type">SlotTag, OldInstance</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">Fires after unequip replication reaches clients.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="callout callout-info">
      <span class="callout-icon">
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"/><line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"/></svg>
      </span>
      <span>Visual actors are spawned server-side and replicated to all clients with <code>COND_None</code>. Cast the result of <code>GetSlotVisual</code> to your actor class (e.g. <code>ACascadeWeaponActor</code>) to access weapon-specific logic on both server and client.</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Wallet Component ───────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="doc-section" id="wallet-component" data-section="wallet-component">
    <h2 class="doc-section-title">
      <span class="section-icon">
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="2" y="5" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/><line x1="2" y1="10" x2="22" y2="10"/></svg>
      </span>
      Wallet Component
    </h2>
    <div class="section-divider"></div>
    <p class="doc-p">
      <strong>UGearWalletComponent</strong> is a tag-keyed currency store. Any number of currency types are supported, each identified by a Gameplay Tag. Multi-currency cost checks and atomic payment are first-class — <code>CanAfford</code> and <code>PayCost</code> operate on a whole cost map, making vendor transactions and recipe costs straightforward.
    </p>

    <table class="prop-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Function</th><th>Description</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td class="prop-name">AddCurrency(CurrencyTag, Amount)</td><td class="prop-desc">Adds <code>Amount</code> to the given currency. Server only.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="prop-name">RemoveCurrency(CurrencyTag, Amount)</td><td class="prop-desc">Removes <code>Amount</code>. Returns false if insufficient. Server only.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="prop-name">HasCurrency(CurrencyTag, Amount)</td><td class="prop-desc">Returns true if at least <code>Amount</code> is present for that tag.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="prop-name">GetCurrency(CurrencyTag)</td><td class="prop-desc">Returns current balance, or 0 if the tag has never been added.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="prop-name">CanAfford(TMap&lt;FGameplayTag,int32&gt;)</td><td class="prop-desc">Returns true if all entries in the cost map can be met simultaneously.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="prop-name">PayCost(TMap&lt;FGameplayTag,int32&gt;)</td><td class="prop-desc">Deducts all entries atomically. Returns false (no change applied) if any single entry is insufficient. Server only.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="prop-name">GetCurrencies()</td><td class="prop-desc">Returns all currency entries as a snapshot array.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="prop-name">ClearAllCurrencies()</td><td class="prop-desc">Removes all currencies. Server only.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <table class="prop-table" style="margin-top:16px">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Delegate</th><th>Parameters</th><th>Description</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td class="prop-name">OnCurrencyChanged</td>
          <td class="prop-type">CurrencyTag, NewAmount</td>
          <td class="prop-desc">Fires on client after replication. Use to refresh currency UI without polling.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Crafting Component ─────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="doc-section" id="crafting-component" data-section="crafting-component">
    <h2 class="doc-section-title">
      <span class="section-icon">
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14.7 6.3a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.4l1.6 1.6a1 1 0 0 0 1.4 0l3.77-3.77a6 6 0 0 1-7.94 7.94l-6.91 6.91a2.12 2.12 0 0 1-3-3l6.91-6.91a6 6 0 0 1 7.94-7.94l-3.76 3.76z"/></svg>
      </span>
      Crafting Component
    </h2>
    <div class="section-divider"></div>
    <p class="doc-p">
      <strong>UGearCraftingComponent</strong> manages known recipes and executes crafts against a provided storage component. It can be placed on a player character for personal crafting or on a workbench actor for station crafting — the caller supplies the source and output storage, so the component is agnostic about where items come from and go.
    </p>

    <div class="doc-subsection">
      <h3 class="doc-subsection-title">Properties</h3>
      <table class="prop-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Property</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name">AvailableRecipes</td>
            <td class="prop-type">TArray&lt;UGearCraftingRecipeDataAsset*&gt;</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">The set of recipes this component knows. Replicated to the owner only.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name">CraftingRule</td>
            <td class="prop-type">UGearCraftingRule*</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">Custom validation logic object. The default rule checks ingredient quantities. Subclass for positional grids, skill requirements, or other conditions.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-subsection">
      <h3 class="doc-subsection-title">Functions</h3>
      <table class="prop-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Function</th><th>Description</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">Craft(Recipe, SourceStorage, OutputStorage)</td><td class="prop-desc">Validates via <code>CanCraft</code>, removes ingredients from <code>SourceStorage</code>, and delivers outputs to <code>OutputStorage</code>. Server only.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">CanCraft(Recipe, SourceStorage)</td><td class="prop-desc">Returns true if all ingredients can be satisfied from <code>SourceStorage</code> without consuming anything.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">GetAvailableRecipes()</td><td class="prop-desc">Returns all known recipes.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">GetCraftableRecipes(SourceStorage)</td><td class="prop-desc">Returns the subset of known recipes that pass <code>CanCraft</code> against the given storage.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">AddRecipe(Recipe)</td><td class="prop-desc">Adds a recipe at runtime — use for discovery systems. Replicated to owner.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">RemoveRecipe(Recipe)</td><td class="prop-desc">Removes a known recipe. Replicated to owner.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-subsection">
      <h3 class="doc-subsection-title">Delegates</h3>
      <table class="prop-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Delegate</th><th>Parameters</th><th>Description</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name">OnCraftingCompleted</td>
            <td class="prop-type">Recipe</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">Fires on the server after a successful craft. Use to play VFX, grant XP, or trigger other game systems.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name">OnCraftingFailed</td>
            <td class="prop-type">Recipe</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">Fires when <code>CanCraft</code> returns false. Provides the recipe so the UI can communicate the specific failure reason.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Recipes ────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="doc-section" id="recipes" data-section="recipes">
    <h2 class="doc-section-title">
      <span class="section-icon">
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 19.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 17H20"/><path d="M6.5 2H20v20H6.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 4 19.5v-15A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 2z"/></svg>
      </span>
      Recipes
    </h2>
    <div class="section-divider"></div>
    <p class="doc-p">
      A <strong>UGearCraftingRecipeDataAsset</strong> declares what is consumed and what is produced. Items are referenced by direct <code>UGearItemDefinition</code> pointer — not by tag — so renaming or moving assets never breaks recipe references. Multiple outputs allow byproduct modelling (e.g. smelting ore yields ingots and slag).
    </p>

    <table class="prop-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Property</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td class="prop-name">Inputs</td>
          <td class="prop-type">TArray&lt;FGearCraftingIngredient&gt;</td>
          <td class="prop-desc">Required items. Each entry: a data asset reference and the required quantity.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="prop-name">Outputs</td>
          <td class="prop-type">TArray&lt;FGearCraftingOutput&gt;</td>
          <td class="prop-desc">Produced items. Each entry: a data asset reference and the quantity to add. Multiple entries enable byproduct drops.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Loot Tables ────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="doc-section" id="loot-tables" data-section="loot-tables">
    <h2 class="doc-section-title">
      <span class="section-icon">
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2"/><path d="M3 9h18M9 21V9"/></svg>
      </span>
      Loot Tables
    </h2>
    <div class="section-divider"></div>
    <p class="doc-p">
      <strong>UGearLootTableDataAsset</strong> is a weighted pool for procedural inventory population. Define a set of entries each with a weight and quantity range, then call <code>UGearFunctionLibrary::PopulateFromLootTable</code> to roll the table and add results directly to a storage component — useful for populating chest contents, enemy drops, and random shop stock.
    </p>

    <table class="prop-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Property</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td class="prop-name">Entries</td>
          <td class="prop-type">TArray&lt;FGearLootEntry&gt;</td>
          <td class="prop-desc">Each entry has: <strong>Item</strong> (UGearItemDefinition*), <strong>Weight</strong> (float), <strong>MinQuantity</strong> (int32), <strong>MaxQuantity</strong> (int32). Higher weight increases the chance of being selected on each roll.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="prop-name">RollCount</td>
          <td class="prop-type">int32</td>
          <td class="prop-desc">Number of items to roll from the pool. Each roll is independent — the same entry can be selected multiple times.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Pickup Actor ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="doc-section" id="pickup-actor" data-section="pickup-actor">
    <h2 class="doc-section-title">
      <span class="section-icon">
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><polyline points="16 12 12 8 8 12"/><line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12" y2="8"/></svg>
      </span>
      Pickup Actor
    </h2>
    <div class="section-divider"></div>
    <p class="doc-p">
      <strong>AGearPickupActor</strong> is the world-space item drop. The pickup actor class and world mesh are configured per item via <code>UGearPickupFragment</code>. It triggers pickup on overlap or on an explicit call and supports configurable lifetimes. Spawn it via <code>UGearFunctionLibrary::DropItem</code> — items without a <code>UGearPickupFragment</code> cannot be dropped. Place a subclass in the editor and call <code>InitializePickup</code> at BeginPlay for pre-placed world pickups.
    </p>

    <div class="doc-subsection">
      <h3 class="doc-subsection-title">Properties</h3>
      <table class="prop-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Property</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name">ItemInstance</td>
            <td class="prop-type">UGearItemInstance*</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">The item this pickup represents. Replicated so clients can display the correct icon before picking up.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name">Quantity</td>
            <td class="prop-type">int32</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">How many units of the item this pickup contains.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name">bAutoPickup</td>
            <td class="prop-type">bool</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">When true, automatically calls <code>Pickup</code> when a UGearStorageComponent overlaps the sphere.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name">PickupRadius</td>
            <td class="prop-type">float</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">Radius of the overlap sphere used for auto-pickup detection.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name">LifetimeMode</td>
            <td class="prop-type">EGearPickupLifetime</td>
            <td class="prop-desc"><span class="badge badge-blue">Persistent</span> never expires. <span class="badge badge-amber">Timed</span> destroys after <code>LifetimeDuration</code> seconds. <span class="badge badge-green">ProjectDefined</span> delegates expiry to your project code.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name">LifetimeDuration</td>
            <td class="prop-type">float</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">Seconds before the pickup expires when <code>LifetimeMode</code> is Timed.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-subsection">
      <h3 class="doc-subsection-title">Functions</h3>
      <table class="prop-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Function</th><th>Description</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">InitializePickup(Definition, Count)</td><td class="prop-desc">Creates a new instance from the definition and sets it on the actor. Use when spawning fresh drops.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">InitializePickupFromInstance(Instance, Count)</td><td class="prop-desc">Uses a pre-created instance — preserves per-instance state such as durability or enchantments when dropping equipped items.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="prop-name">Pickup(Instigator)</td><td class="prop-desc">Adds the item to the first <code>UGearStorageComponent</code> found on the Instigator actor. Destroys the pickup on success.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-subsection">
      <h3 class="doc-subsection-title">Delegates</h3>
      <table class="prop-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Delegate</th><th>Parameters</th><th>Description</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name">OnPickedUp</td>
            <td class="prop-type">PickupActor, Instigator</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">Fires when the item is successfully added to the instigator's storage. Use to play pickup SFX or show a notification.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="prop-name">OnLifetimeExpired</td>
            <td class="prop-type">PickupActor</td>
            <td class="prop-desc">Fires when the Timed lifetime elapses before pickup. Use to play a despawn effect.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Transfer System ────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="doc-section" id="transfer-system" data-section="transfer-system">
    <h2 class="doc-section-title">
      <span class="section-icon">
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
      </span>
      Transfer System
    </h2>
    <div class="section-divider"></div>
    <p class="doc-p">
      <strong>UGearFunctionLibrary</strong> is a static function library for all cross-component item movement. Every item transfer in GearFlow — looting a chest, buying from a vendor, dropping an item to the world — runs through one of these functions. The unified model means one set of delegates fires on both endpoints, and no custom item-movement code is needed in your project.
    </p>

    <div class="code-block">
      <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-lang">C++</span></div>
      <pre><code><span class="code-comment">// Loot a chest into player inventory</span>
UGearFunctionLibrary::TransferItem(ChestInventory, PlayerInventory, Item, Count);

<span class="code-comment">// Buy from vendor (deducts Cost from wallet)</span>
UGearFunctionLibrary::TransferItem(VendorInventory, PlayerInventory, Item, 1, PlayerWallet);

<span class="code-comment">// Drop item to world</span>
UGearFunctionLibrary::DropItem(WorldContext, PlayerInventory, Item, 1, DropTransform);</code></pre>
    </div>

    <table class="prop-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Function</th><th>Description</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td class="prop-name">TransferItem(From, To, Item, Count, Wallet)</td>
          <td class="prop-desc">Moves Count units from <code>From</code> to <code>To</code>. If <code>Wallet</code> is provided and the item carries a <code>UGearCostFragment</code>, deducts the cost map first — the transfer fails atomically if the wallet cannot cover all currencies. Server only.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="prop-name">PopulateFromLootTable(Storage, LootTable)</td>
          <td class="prop-desc">Rolls the loot table and adds results to <code>Storage</code>. Returns the number of items actually added.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="prop-name">DropItem(WorldContext, Storage, Item, Count, Transform)</td>
          <td class="prop-desc">Removes the item from <code>Storage</code> and spawns a pickup actor at <code>Transform</code>. The actor class is determined by the item's <code>UGearPickupFragment</code>. Returns nullptr if the item has no <code>UGearPickupFragment</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="prop-name">DropItemInstance(WorldContext, Storage, Instance, Transform)</td>
          <td class="prop-desc">Drops a specific instance — preserves per-instance state (durability, enchantments, etc.) on the spawned pickup actor. Returns nullptr if the item has no <code>UGearPickupFragment</code>.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <div class="callout callout-info">
      <span class="callout-icon">
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"/><line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"/></svg>
      </span>
      <span>All <code>TransferItem</code> paths call <code>UGearStorageComponent::AddItem</code> and <code>RemoveItem</code> internally, so <code>OnSlotChanged</code> delegates fire normally on both the source and destination components.</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Multiplayer ────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="doc-section" id="multiplayer" data-section="multiplayer">
    <h2 class="doc-section-title">
      <span class="section-icon">
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M17 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H5a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/><path d="M23 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"/><path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"/></svg>
      </span>
      Replication
    </h2>
    <div class="section-divider"></div>
    <p class="doc-p">
      All three storage components — Inventory, Equipment, and Wallet — use <strong>FastArray replication</strong> with delta compression. Only changed slot entries are transmitted per frame; a 100-slot inventory that receives one item sends roughly 20–30 bytes, not a full array snapshot. The replication model is <strong>server-authoritative</strong> — all mutating functions must originate on the server. Client-side calls are silently ignored. The recommended pattern is: client sends a Server RPC → server validates and mutates → FastArray replicates the delta → delegates fire on client with the new state.
    </p>

    <div class="feature-grid">
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="22 12 18 12 15 21 9 3 6 12 2 12"/></svg>
        </div>
        <p class="feature-title">Delta Compression</p>
        <p class="feature-desc">FastArray sends only the slot entries that changed since the last ACK. Full snapshots are never retransmitted after the initial connection sync.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="11" rx="2" ry="2"/><path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4"/></svg>
        </div>
        <p class="feature-title">Server Authoritative</p>
        <p class="feature-desc">Inventory state lives on the server. Clients receive replicated copies. No client can forge an item grant or craft result.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>
        </div>
        <p class="feature-title">Visual Replication</p>
        <p class="feature-desc">Equipment visual actors are spawned server-side and replicated to all clients with <code>COND_None</code>, so every player sees the correct visual without extra RPC code.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M18 8h1a4 4 0 0 1 0 8h-1"/><path d="M2 8h16v9a4 4 0 0 1-4 4H6a4 4 0 0 1-4-4V8z"/><line x1="6" y1="1" x2="6" y2="4"/><line x1="10" y1="1" x2="10" y2="4"/><line x1="14" y1="1" x2="14" y2="4"/></svg>
        </div>
        <p class="feature-title">Delegates on Client</p>
        <p class="feature-desc"><code>OnSlotChanged</code>, <code>OnItemEquipped</code>, and <code>OnCurrencyChanged</code> all fire on the client after replication, making UI bindings straightforward.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</PluginLayout>

